TITLE:: SpiralPanel
summary:: Spiral's device panel
categories:: Libraries>Spiral
related:: Classes/Spiral, Classes/SpiralView, Classes/SpiralShiftKnob, Classes/FxDevicePanel

DESCRIPTION::
The link::Classes/FxDevicePanel:: every effect of the family has, plus two things: its shift knob is a link::Classes/SpiralShiftKnob::, which says the shift with its sign, and it hands the display the panel, so hovering a part of the link::Classes/SpiralView:: lights the knobs that set it, and hovering one of those knobs lights its part of the display. code::Spiral.panelClass:: answers it, so code::p.gui:: and code::p.panel(view):: both use it.

code::
p = Spiral.new;
p.gui;                                   // the window, with a SpiralPanel in it

(
// or the same panel in a window of yours
w = Window("spiral", Rect(100, 100, 960, 580));
q = p.panel(w.view);
w.view.layout = VLayout(q.view);
q.running = true;                        // meters on while it shows
w.onClose = { q.remove };
w.front;
);
::

